Z||000006||Majik||07-20-2000||05:55 PM||||I got my 86 GT at a local (rinky-dink) used car lot.  The car had no clutch (how did they think they were going to sell it).  I picked it up for 1450 (in pretty good condition, except for the exterior needing paint.  He wanted to sell it for 2050, but I told him he was out of his mind...the only thing I wanted to do was save a fiero...and get me my ride  (c:  I probally paid too much for it, but hey, its the car I've wanted for a long long time...<P>Majik||||reg||1
Z||000007||Old Lar||07-20-2000||06:32 PM||||You missed the sale was a bit I got told on a car. (a used stripped Escort wagon, 4 year old 27000 miles)  I had the paper with the ad and I offered a couple of hundred bucks under the sale price.  He groaned, but I got it for the price cause a stripped (5 speed manual, no radio)Escort wouldn't sell no matter what.<P>The last car I traded in, I got $3K on paper and saw it on the used car lot: "Price just reduced from $6495 to $5200".  I wondered what it really sold for.  Blue book wholesale was only $3K.<P>I'd offer $1500 cash.  Only a few select Fiero customers out there.||||reg||1
Z||000008||286SE'S||07-20-2000||06:57 PM||||Two years ago I saw a beautiful 87 Gt at the (look-at-me spot) raised corner pedistal  of the dealer I bought my 86 2M4. Had to stop and look it over. It was White/Tan interior and Wow was it clean it had 57,000 mile and was priced at $5995.00. I told myself it wasn't what I wanted because it was an auto but it sure was tempting. Three days later it was gone. If a car is really clean it will sell fast.<BR>Terry||||reg||1
Z||000009||batboy||07-20-2000||07:18 PM||||The salesman is telling you that it'll sale for $1995, that's the starting price to me.||||reg||1
Z||000010||fieroshop||07-20-2000||11:39 PM||||Buying a Fiero and asking what is a fair price is a little bit much since most everybody wants to tell you what to pay for it ofcourse they are not in the market for a new Fiero. There are a lot a deals out there but remember that a Fiero is worth what you are willing to pay. I mean I bought an 87 GT that was wreck and all it was good for was a parts car, I paid $1000.00 for it. Granted I had two customers who needed parts. One bought the getrag and the other the engine. I also had the pleasure of doing the installs.So if you think the car is worth 2500.00 or 1000.00 dollars, it is only worth it to you and nobody else.<P>------------------<BR> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fieroshop_sig_1.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000011||Terrybogin||07-21-2000||12:16 AM||||If it was "on sale" at $1995, then that is what I would offer for the car. There are too many of these cars around to get ripped for $1000 more than the sale price.||||reg||1
Z||000012||loafer87gt||07-21-2000||01:11 AM||||I saw a beautifull red 88 GT in the paper so I went and checked it out. It had 24000 miles on it, and the guy was asking $17500 for it. I thought this was WAAAY to high, even it is a low mileage GT. ||||reg||1
Z||000013||DJRice||07-21-2000||08:45 AM||||I bet $1500-$1700 cash money gets you the car.  If that car was on sale a couple of days before, its still on sale now.  Especially where cash is concerned.<P>------------------<BR>Dillon - Titusville, FL<BR>Black '87 SE V6<BR>"Matched Perfect and Staggered Special"||||reg||1
Z||000014||trigger||07-21-2000||09:50 AM||||Hi,<BR>There is an 87 Coupe 4Cyl. 5Spd. for sale at a used lot in Monticello, Iowa.  It is called Freeze Motors.  I'm not sure about the miles but it is Maroon and the paint is shot.  The speakers are blown and it has no options.  Not even cruise.  It might have air.  It has seat covers and we didn't look under them.  When my dad and I went to drive it the battery was dead.  He is asking $3,000 for it.  I think that is way to much.  Have fun all.  Bye.||||reg||1
Z||000015||Philphine||07-21-2000||10:28 AM||||i bought my '87 for $1999 about 3 years ago. same deal. it had been on the lot a while and was originally $2999. about 109,000 mls. just recently got an indy off ebay for $1300 but it needs repair. <P>now looking at an '84 at a dav car lot. i mentioned it here a few months back. paint bad but no damage, dosen't even look scratched, just faded really bad. interior has same kinda faded look but only damage is the usual drivers seat rip. window says it needs a fuel pump. should be about $250 or less going by what they said a few weeks back. gonna give it a more serious look today and decide if i want to get it. <P>------------------<P><BR>'87 coupe (feral)<BR>'84 indy<P>a 4 cyl. is pretty easy to find in louisville. come to the show (if you're close) and buy a bargain mart (the local swap and shop paper). always 1 or 2 in there and a few on various car lots in the city.<P>[This message has been edited by Philphine (edited 07-21-2000).]<p>[This message has been edited by Philphine (edited 07-21-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000016||Monkeyman||07-21-2000||10:50 AM||||Money talks and bullsh** walks.  Flash the salesman $1500 cold, hard cash and drive away in a Fiero.<P>There was an '87 GT for sale in the Trader recently.  17k miles, "custom" for $27,000US.  I actually called they guy thinking he had made a mistake in the price.  Nope.  Right price.  I asked what was custom about it.  He said it had an aftermarket stereo.  Whoopee.  What a lunatic.||||reg||1
Z||000017||b lo 0||07-21-2000||12:00 PM||||In my opinion, never, EVER buy a used car from a dealer.  I got my '85 GT, 145,000 miles, in perfect mechanical condition, but needing a repaint and windshield, for $1,500.  That's with automatic, power windows, door locks, and trunk release, cruise, A/C, new tape player and a 10-disc CD changer, new tires, and all service records, ETC.  I think I got hooked up on this deal.  If you poke around (I found it in the newspaper) you can find a great deal like this.  Take my advice.  The only car I ever got from a dealer was an '89 4runner in 1990 as a left over and spent over $27,000 on it.  It's only worth about 5 grand now.  Anyways, keep your eyes open, and you shall recieve...or something like that.  Happy Fiero-ing!!<P>------------------<BR>'85 GT (in progress)  <BR>titled ICE-plates B LO 0 <BR>GAWD I love this car||||reg||1
Z||000018||stsmithgt||07-21-2000||01:57 PM||||HEY!  There's a lot better deals out there than that.  I picked up my white 86GT with $2000.00  I think the only thing it doesn't have is the leather interier.  Everything works and looks great with 73,000 miles on it.  Now it has 115,000 and yes, in the last 4 years I have sunk a lot of money into it to maintain it's spunk and appeal. Where was I going with this? Oh yeah, rock him with a low price (1300?)and make sure to point out all the bad stuff that has to be fixed like probably motormounts, clutch, struts and scratch or pitted glass.  A car with that many miles on it has to have something wrong with it or it wouldn't be at the dealership.  Things like that should knock down the price. I just spent my 2 cents----NEXT!||||reg||1
Z||000019||Philphine||07-23-2000||11:58 PM||||bought the car.$125. also got a bargain mart. 2 4cyls. less than $1000, '85 gt for $2500. also 2 on a couple of car lots near me, one i see near where i work ('88 4cyl. don't remember price but i think it was kind of high), one offered to me fairly cheap, $500, by a local garage when he heard i liked fieros, and one kind of customised one (frog eye lights, arturo front) that is near where i work but i haven't seen it in a few weeks, might be sold.<P>thats without really tryin'. <p>[This message has been edited by Philphine (edited 07-24-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000020||My7Fieros||07-24-2000||03:15 AM||||The most Ive paid for any of my Fieros is $2400..that was for the first one...an 86 SE V6 4 speed w/ 70K miles...it was (and still is) in MINT condition. Then I bought an 86 GT at a Honda dealership..62K miles!...it had just been traded in, needed nothing more than alittle tlc...I gave it the basic tune up, fixed the temp.needle (it fell off, go figure) and painted it...paid $2000 total out the door.<BR>I bought my Formula for $850!!! Of course it was in rough shape, and Im STILL working on it after 6 months (only cosmetics now, getting ready to paint it and I'll be FINISHED with it!)..(oh yeah, right at 100K miles)....<BR>Then I bought another 86 SE V6 auto,121k miles, excellent (almost mint) condition, gave it the usual tune up...paid $1100<BR>Next came the 4banger t-topper, bought it sight unseen...unfortunantly, even for me, it was too far gone, so I had to (cringe) part it (by the way, Ive got the glass ttops if anyone is interested)...paid $200 (yes, two hundred)<BR>Then came the next 86 SE V6 auto...needed a fuel pump...had a mechanics lean...he wanted it gone, so I gave him $225!(of course it has 186k miles!)<BR>Then I bought an 87 GT,(82K miles) SUPER condition except for the high idle which I have yet to find....paid $1400 at an auction.<BR>So, all you have to do is look, and definantly hassle the seller...they'll come down on the price, believe me!    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>Btw, I still have EVERY one of these! Count'em, 7, hence my screen name. I love these cars! will it ever end?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>[This message has been edited by My7Fieros (edited 07-24-2000).]<p>[This message has been edited by My7Fieros (edited 07-24-2000).]||||reg||4
